 160: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
 161:     """Recolor the small defect bars on each shared-color object with the opposite panel color.
 162: 
 163:     Input structure
 164:     - The grid contains two large panel colors and one shared object color.
 165:     - Each shared-color object is a mostly solid rectangle inside exactly one panel.
 166:     Rule
 167:     - Find the near-solid rectangular core of each object.
 168:     - Missing core pixels and one-cell protrusions define two-pixel bars perpendicular to the nearest core edge.
 169:     - Recolor those bars with the other panel color; leave all other pixels unchanged.
 170:     Key insight
 171:     - The colors to add are not tied to numeric ids: each object's surrounding panel identifies the opposite panel color.
 172:     """
